+# Guarded companion API
+
+`GET /api/v1/companion` and `POST /api/v1/companion` require `Authorization: Bearer <STS2_COMPANION_TOKEN>`. Set this environment variable before launching the game. The raw multiplayer API keeps its original behavior.
+
+Every POST contains `instance_id`, `run_id`, `local_player_id` (NetId string), `version`, a unique `action_id`, `expires_at` (ISO 8601 with offset; at most 30 seconds ahead), `action`, and the parameters below. Send the exact identities/version obtained from GET. Body limit: 32 KiB.
+
+The response envelope contains `state`, `allowed_actions`, `receipt`, recent `receipts`, `pending_action_id`, and `requires_reconciliation`. GET `?action_id=...` retrieves a specific receipt. An `accepted` receipt means dispatch only. Wait for its `effect_observed=true` before submitting another action. A transport timeout or an `uncertain` receipt must never be retried using a fresh ID. An identical ID/payload returns the original receipt; a changed payload with that ID is rejected.
+
+An exact local `PlayCardAction` that finishes after cancellation before entering `CardModel.SpendResources` can settle as `status="not_executed"`, `reason="play_card_cancelled_before_resources"`, `effect_observed=false`, `requires_reconciliation=false`, with `observed_version` set to the confirming readback. This clears its pending gate, including when the evidence arrives after an `uncertain` timeout. The old action ID remains idempotent: observe the current state and make a new decision instead of replaying it. Resource-boundary entry, missing exact action identity, incomplete/faulted execution, or absence of cancellation evidence keeps the outcome uncertain. Hosts retain the exact submitted action object. Clients associate all locally sent ordinary actions, including manual actions, with their reliable ordered host echoes using a FIFO scoped to the game synchronizer. Only the next echo may consume the next request; the full serialized action and run location must match. Missing or mismatched echoes, failed sends, or disconnected sends invalidate correlation for that synchronizer instead of searching for a similar card/target. This uses the native protocol without adding or changing packets.
+
+## Actions and local effect evidence
+
+| Action | Parameters | Required local state | Effect evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `play_card` | `card_index`, `target` when needed | combat play phase | Exact card leaves hand after resources start, with completed play task or pending local selection |
+| `end_turn` | none | combat play phase, not ready | Valid authoritative local end-turn execution, or same-combat/round local ready state |
+| `use_potion` | `slot`, `target` when needed | potion usable | Exact potion leaves its local slot and is no longer queued |
+| `discard_potion` | `slot` | occupied local slot | Exact potion leaves slot and is no longer queued |
+| `choose_map_node` | `index` in `map.next_options` | map, new local vote | Exact player/source/coordinate/map-generation vote recorded by synchronizer |
+| `claim_reward` | `index` in `rewards.items` | rewards | Reward reports successful selection, its own card reward screen opens, or removal choice opens |
+| `select_card_reward` | `card_index` in `card_reward.cards` | card reward | Exact selected card object appears in local deck |
+| `skip_card_reward` | none | card reward with `can_skip` | Local card reward screen closes |
+| `proceed` | none | enabled proceed in rewards/rest/shop/fake merchant/treasure | Local map opens |
+| `choose_event_option` | `index` in `event.options` | event; visible, enabled, unlocked, not chosen | Shared choice: exact local vote; individual choice: corresponding option task completes or opens a selection; proceed option: its task completes and the local map opens |
+| `advance_dialogue` | none | event with `in_dialogue` | Local dialogue line advances or dialogue closes |
+| `choose_rest_option` | `index` in `rest_site.options` | visible enabled rest choice | Corresponding local rest task completes with proceed enabled, or opens a selection |
+| `select_card` | `index` in `card_select.cards` | card selection, no preview yet | Exact card toggles selection, local preview changes, or selection task completes |
+| `confirm_selection` | none | `card_select.can_confirm` | Local selection task completes |
+| `cancel_selection` | none | `card_select.can_cancel` | Selection closes or preview returns to choosing |
+| `open_shop` | none | shop/fake merchant, inventory closed | Local inventory opens |
+| `close_shop` | none | shop/fake merchant, inventory open | Local inventory closes |
+| `shop_purchase` | `index` in shop items | inventory open, stocked, affordable | Local purchase task returns success after effects/hooks, or opens a selection |
+| `open_treasure` | none | treasure with `can_open_chest` | Relic collection becomes visible or proceed becomes enabled |
+| `claim_treasure_relic` | `index` in `treasure.relics` | opened treasure collection | Authoritative `OnPicked` for exact local player, relic offer, and relic index |
+
+Menus, profile changes, load/abandon, undo end turn, and unlisted actions are rejected. Blocking FTUE/popups must be handled manually before companion actions. The local UI and ownership checks run on the game thread immediately before dispatch.
+
+## Read-only state and adapter fields
+
+2026-10-24 companion additions:
+
+- `state.game_version`: the running executable's `release_info.json` version; null if unavailable, never an assumed release.
+- `state.combat_in_progress`: native combat activity. A combat room can remain visible briefly while rewards load; it is not by itself a finished battle result.
+- `player.hand[].dynamic_vars`: native base values, not final predictions. `adviser_rule` is set only for audited, unenchanted, unreplayed Ironclad Strike/Defend; modifiers still require separate checks.
+- Combat `players[].status` and bounded relic descriptions expose public teammate modifiers.
+- `state_type=game_over` includes `game_over.win` from the current native room's victory flag when available; null is unknown.
+- A `play_card` receipt waits for the exact associated play task to complete successfully, as well as leaving hand and idle hand UI. A still-pending task may instead acknowledge reaching a local card-selection screen so that its next choice can proceed. This does not claim that the unresolved choice has finished the full card effect.
+
+Companion GET uses the existing multiplayer state shape while disabling legacy auto-open side effects. It never clicks a treasure chest, opens a merchant inventory, or opens the fake merchant inventory. Explicit open/close actions are required.
+
+- `player.deck`: local deck card details.
+- `shop.inventory_open`: normal merchant inventory visibility; `null` while the matching local shop UI is loading, so no open/close action is available yet.
+- `fake_merchant.inventory_open`; its items/proceed flag remain under `fake_merchant.shop`.
+- `treasure.can_open_chest`: explicit chest-opening availability.
+- `treasure.bids[].voted` and `vote_relic_index`: primitive fields, correcting the legacy serializer's opaque vote object. **Local bids can be predicted UI votes; only the receipt proves authoritative confirmation.**
+- `card_select.selected_indices`: selected cards on supported grid selection screens.
+- `card_reward.cards[].can_select` and `card_select.cards[].can_select`: actual local clickability, including the game's 350 ms reward opening delay. Wait when false.
+- `event.options[].is_enabled`: actual local visible/enabled state; `rest_site.options[].is_enabled` also requires the ready UI for the exact local room and its matching option button. While the rest scene/buttons are loading, all rest options and `can_proceed` are false.
+- `event.dialogue_line`: ancient dialogue line number.
+
+Common transitions: `rewards -> card_reward -> rewards -> map`; `event -> card_select -> event`; `rest_site -> card_select -> rest_site -> map`. A shared event/map/treasure vote can leave the current screen visible while waiting for teammates. Do not repeat a recorded local vote. Ordinary event proceed options use `choose_event_option`, not `proceed`. Close a shop before `proceed`.
+
+## Verification scope
+
+The ledger is tested outside the game for idempotency, expiry, stale identity/version rejection, pending serialization, uncertain outcomes, and all 20 action names. Installed-game reflection checks verify the private fields/methods used by observation hooks and selection readers. The native multiplayer progression test is a separate required acceptance step: unit/reflection checks do not establish game animation, reward, event, or network behavior.
+
+Expected effects that are not observed within 10 seconds become uncertain and block further guarded submissions for that run. Hooks never treat a teammate's generic state change or a queued acknowledgement as completion. A hook unavailable after a game update may conservatively leave a receipt unresolved; do not bypass it by generating another action ID.
